- [ ] **Boss key** (user idea, 2026-08-13). One keypress hides the game behind something innocuous. **A browser cannot minimize its own window** — `window.minimize()` does not exist, `moveTo`/`resizeTo` only apply to windows the page itself opened via `window.open`, and `window.close()` likewise. Pages get no control over browser chrome at all, so the disguise has to happen *inside* the page. That is the whole constraint; everything else here is easy.
  - **The engine half is already built, which is the thing worth knowing before scoping this.** A real pause exists: `simulate()` early-returns on `local.isPaused` (`engine.ts:~2635`) and `this.levelTime += dt` is at `~2772`, i.e. **after** the gate — so pausing freezes the level clock too and spike traps cannot desync across it. It is toggled by Escape and, more usefully here, **`blur` and pointer-unlock already force it true**, so alt-tabbing away has always paused the game. Nothing in the sim needs changing; this is a presentation feature.
  - **What actually has to be built**, in rough order of how much of the effect each buys:
    1. **The overlay.** The only part that does real work. On-theme option that beats a generic fake spreadsheet: the level was *generated from a real source file*, so show that file, syntax-highlighted — a plausible thing to be looking at, and the data is already on hand. The console sidebar is an existing code-shaped surface to borrow styling from.
    2. **`document.exitFullscreen()`.** Allowed without a user gesture. Load-bearing: a boss key that leaves a *fullscreen* fake IDE up is more conspicuous than the game was.
    3. **Tab title + favicon swap.** The tab strip gives it away otherwise.
    4. **Audio.** `bgm.ts` has `pause()`; procedural SFX stop on their own once the sim is frozen, but confirm rather than assume — `notifyFrozen` fires on the edge and may already be wired.
  - **Key choice needs a real physical keypress to validate, not synthetic events.** This repo already has the scar: `Ctrl+W` turned out to be an unblockable browser-level shortcut that no amount of synthetic `KeyboardEvent` testing caught, and the same class of risk was flagged again for `Alt+Enter` in the reload item below. Taken already: `Escape` (pause), `Tab` (automap), `Backquote` (fire — also the bot's), `KeyE`/`KeyF`/`KeyR`, `ShiftRight`. Browser-reserved: F1/F3/F5/F11/F12 and `Ctrl`-anything worth having. F8/F9 look free, which is exactly the claim to test by hand.
  - **The same key toggles back out** (user, 2026-08-13). Straightforward as a flag, but four details decide whether it feels right, and three of them are about *not* doing things:
    1. **Do not auto-resume the sim.** Un-bossing should reveal the game still **paused**, not drop the player back into a fight with whatever was standing next to them. The existing flow already handles the rest: `simulate()` resumes on `local.isPaused && clicked`, and `onCanvasClick` (`input.ts`) already calls `requestPointerLock()`. Boss mode hands back to that and does nothing itself.
    2. **Do not try to restore pointer lock directly.** The click path above already does it correctly, and a re-lock attempted straight after an Escape-driven exit is blocked by the browser on purpose — `onPointerLockChange`'s doc comment covers why that whole area resists being driven from script.
    3. **Restoring fullscreen *is* allowed, but only synchronously in the keydown handler.** `requestFullscreen()` needs a user gesture and the un-boss keypress is one — that gesture is spent if it is awaited first. Only relevant if boss mode took fullscreen away in the first place, so remember whether it did rather than unconditionally re-entering.
    4. **Save and restore the tab title/favicon rather than hardcoding them back.** The title carries campaign/level context, so the "restore" value has to be captured at boss time.
  - **Two ordering/precedence calls to make deliberately rather than discover:** audio should die *before* the overlay appears and come back *after* it is gone, or the transition leaks in whichever direction lags; and `Escape` currently toggles pause, so decide whether it also dismisses boss mode (panic-safety, at the cost of a double meaning) or is swallowed while it is up.
  - **This argues for a function key over a letter**, on top of the reserved-key problem: the disguise is a focusable code-ish surface, and a fake editor that eats letter keys would swallow its own dismiss key.
  - **Blind spot, per the bot-automation note below**: bots never blur, never click and never leave fullscreen, so *none* of this is reachable by any bot-driven test. It needs manual verification or nothing.

